I fixed #1112 and committed it as 2900fcad. A flag written after -- is now only prompt text and is no longer also applied. Before this, yoyo -- --no-color hi sent --no-color hi and turned colour off as well.

What changed
• I added a small helper, cli_config::has_option(args, names), which only looks at the flags before -- (the same option_args view #1110 used). Both early scans call it:
  • apply_cli_flags in src/main.rs: --no-color, --no-bell, --no-notify, --no-rtk.
  • The quiet check in parse_args in src/cli.rs: --quiet/-q, --print.
• I checked the other blocks the task asked about. hints_disabled_from and parse_output_flags are only called from parse_args_with_config, after the point where it switches to option_args, so they were already correct.

Tests
• A table test on has_option. A flag before -- still applies, which is the common case. After -- it does not, for --no-color, --no-bell, --quiet, -q and --print. The same test checks the word still reaches the prompt unchanged.
• A real-binary test in tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs, using the existing stub and env-scrubbing helper: yoyo -- --no-color --quiet hi sends all three words in the request.
• Limit: the binary test can't see whether colour or quiet were actually switched, because piped output already turns colour off and quiet on. That decision is covered by the has_option table, since both call sites now go through that function.
• Positive control: I changed has_option to scan all of argv, and the table test failed by name. I restored it in the same command, and no sabotage marker is left in the tree.
• cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

Also done
• Added one sentence to docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md: no flag after -- is applied, including colour, bell, notifications, --quiet and --print.
• src/cli.rs shrank by one line, so I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs to 7872.
• I filed the value-slot case as #1113. I confirmed it at the built binary: yoyo -p --help still prints the help page instead of sending --help as the prompt. Closing #1112 leaves that problem with its own open issue.
• git grep '#1112' src docs only finds the new code comments, which describe the fixed behaviour, so nothing user-facing points at the closed ticket.
